Key moves:
- Pass `isSelected` (a boolean) instead of computing the style in the parent. Primitives are free to compare.
- Hoist constants out of the component.
- `useCallback` the handler so its identity is stable.

One caveat: for 2000 rows, even successful memoization may not be enough. React still has to walk the tree and run the shallow comparison on every row. The structural fix is virtualization — render only the ~30 rows in view. `@tanstack/react-virtual` or `react-window` will give you a bigger win than memo tuning. Memoize first to fix correctness, then virtualize if the profiler still shows long render commits.

