The pattern matching approach prevents several specific issues present in the original code. First, it eliminates the risk of `NullReferenceException` when accessing `dictData["name"]` because the `?.` operator ensures safe navigation. Second, it removes the unsafe cast operations by using `is string name` which both checks type and extracts the value in one operation. Third, the switch expression provides compile-time verification that all code paths return a value, preventing accidental missing cases.

Additionally, the pattern matching syntax is more declarative and self-documenting - each condition clearly expresses what pattern it's matching against rather than requiring readers to parse through multiple nested if-else conditions. The performance is also improved since `GetType()` calls are eliminated in favor of efficient pattern matching at the IL level.

